<!-- Handoff about.html: why. Native Astro markup; shared document shell is V9Layout. -->
<section class="g-dark" id="why">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="eyebrow"><span class="tick">\</span> Why now</div>
    <h2 style="--d:60ms">One hire. 319 applications.</h2>
    <p class="lead" style="--d:120ms">
      In 2021 it was 121. Reaching a candidate has never been cheaper, and deciding on one now takes more interviews
      than it ever has.
    </p>
    <figure
      class="ab-ink"
      id="abInk"
      aria-label="Applications per hire rose from 121 in Q1 2021 to 319 in Q4 2024, and stayed above 300 through 2025."
    >
      <svg viewBox="0 0 1000 300" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true">
        <line class="ab-ink-ax" x1="0" y1="290" x2="1000" y2="290"></line>
        <path
          class="ab-ink-ln"
          pathLength="1"
          vector-effect="non-scaling-stroke"
          d="M40,181 C120,176 200,168 280,150 C380,128 470,96 560,72 C620,56 680,40 730,35.5 C790,31 850,44 914,49.4"
        ></path>
      </svg>
      <i class="ab-ink-pt" style="left:4%;top:60.3%"></i><i class="ab-ink-pt ab-ink-pt--big" style="left:73%;top:11.8%"
      ></i><i class="ab-ink-pt" style="left:91.4%;top:16.5%"></i>
      <span class="ab-ink-n ab-ink-n--a" style="left:4%;top:60.3%"><b>121</b><em>Q1 2021</em></span>
      <span class="ab-ink-n ab-ink-n--b" style="left:73%;top:11.8%"><b>319</b><em>Q4 2024</em></span>
      <span class="ab-ink-n ab-ink-n--c" style="left:91.4%;top:16.5%"><b>still above 300</b><em>through 2025</em></span>
      <span class="ab-ink-yr" style="left:4%">2021</span><span class="ab-ink-yr" style="left:22.4%">2022</span><span
        class="ab-ink-yr"
        style="left:40.8%">2023</span
      ><span class="ab-ink-yr" style="left:59.2%">2024</span><span class="ab-ink-yr" style="left:77.6%">2025</span>
    </figure>
    <p class="ab-ink-2">And each technical hire now takes <b>17.6</b> interviews, up from <b>11.6</b> in 2021.</p>
    <p class="ab-src">
      Applications per hire, all roles. Source: Ashby Talent Trends Report, 2021 to Q1 2026. The line joins the reported
      points.
    </p>
    <div class="proof-checks ab-why">
      <div style="--d:0ms">
        <h3>Sourcing got almost free.</h3><p>
          One person with the right tools can put four hundred profiles in front of a hiring manager in an afternoon.
          That used to take a team a month.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div style="--d:90ms">
        <h3>So the pipeline stopped meaning much.</h3><p>
          Every extra profile lands on the same hiring manager, who still has one calendar and a team waiting on the
          hire.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div style="--d:180ms">
        <h3>Judgment became the scarce part.</h3><p>
          Someone senior, who has done the job, deciding what an answer was worth. No tool has made that cheaper.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="decide decide--d"><b>Everyone automated the finding. We built for the deciding.</b></p>
  </div>
</section>
